{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe","id":1508978,"title":"Something to the SoE","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-19T20:06:57-07:00","id":1508978,"title":"Something to the SoE","content":"It's just a few concepts I thought of seeing how the SoE operates, so I wanted a second opinion to see if I'm getting this right since I don't have much experience with it myself.<br /> <br /> Portable railgun: Basically a weapon composed of a rifle-like cannon, powered by an ether battery on its back and capable of launching large electrical discharges, it would need Prime 2 to generate electricity and Forces from 2 to 4 depending on how much power you use.<br /> <br /> Rocket Backpack: As the name implies, a rocket pack that allows its wielder to fly or at least leave the ground for a while, Prime 2 to create flames and Forces 3 or 4 to control speed.<br /> <br /> Restorative mixture: Basically a chemical formula that would allow anyone to recover from injury. As it involves chemical compounds, Matter 2, and since it involves living beings as well, Life 2 to 4 depending on the potency of the mixture.<br /> <br /> Ether Capsule: Nothing complex actually, using Prime 2 inserts quintessence into a capsule that can be opened to recharge the mage quickly, of course it must be prepared in advance, not sure if it also needed Matter to function.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T00:12:54-07:00","id":1509007,"title":"","content":"While none of these are entirely off-base, there's cleaner ways to handle most of them.<br /> <br /> Rail-guns: Rail-guns don't shoot electric blasts, so you might just need to rename this. A rail-gun, as the name implies, propels an armature down rails, and as the armature stops at the end of the rails, the projectile continues on having gained momentum from sitting in the armature. There are also coil-guns where the electromagnetic field used to accelerate is also used to suspend the projectile; negating the need for an armature or physical rails. These are real things we already have. The most important tool a SoE has to making a functional rail-gun weapon, is Matter. The biggest issue in rail-gun technology in multiple applications is the force of the magnetic acceleration is so strong, rail-guns have to be huge just to avoid ripping themselves to pieces.<br /> <br /> So while some Forces would help make a rail-gun more practical, what you want to start with is some Ether science to cook up some exotic materials via Matter so the actually body of the weapon is light enough to use, and strong enough to be fired more than once. After solving that current tech can handle the rest enough to make a weapon.<br /> <br /> Now, a Scientist! might want to go above and beyond this into creating a plasma rail-gun, that shoots some form of plasma bolt instead of a solid slug. Then you're going to need Forces and Prime to generate your ammo because we have no idea how to do that at human-weapon scales.<br /> <br /> Rocket-packs: So, again, you don't need Prime, because we have rockets (though really you're probably going to want to use jet-packs in how they actually operate). Again, Matter is your friend because one of the reasons these aren't &quot;real&quot; yet is the material engineering side of things more than the physics side of things. One of the biggest problems with making a jet-pack a reality, is carrying enough fuel, so using Matter to vastly increase how much fuel your pack holds without increase weight is going to get you a functional pack better than constantly tried to use Forces and Prime to generate thrust. Matter also helps you make a flight suit that will keep your legs from burning off.<br /> <br /> Restorative mixtures: Now you need Prime, because you're just making a &quot;healing potion&quot; where you're making a Charm via Prime that creates a single use Life 2 self-healing effect for the mage that activates it.<br /> <br /> Ether Capsule: If you're just turning a physical item into Tass, you generally don't need Matter as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T03:22:49-07:00","id":1509017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe#post1508978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just a few concepts I thought of seeing how the SoE operates, so I wanted a second opinion to see if I'm getting this right since I don't have much experience with it myself.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the faction of this Tradition Mage of the Society of the Ether ? Adventurer, Progressivist, or some different group ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T04:59:23-07:00","id":1509027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe#post1508978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just a few concepts I thought of seeing how the SoE operates, so I wanted a second opinion to see if I'm getting this right since I don't have much experience with it myself.<br /> <br /> Portable railgun: Basically a weapon composed of a rifle-like cannon, powered by an ether battery on its back and capable of launching large electrical discharges, it would need Prime 2 to generate electricity and Forces from 2 to 4 depending on how much power you use.<br /> <br /> Rocket Backpack: As the name implies, a rocket pack that allows its wielder to fly or at least leave the ground for a while, Prime 2 to create flames and Forces 3 or 4 to control speed.<br /> <br /> Restorative mixture: Basically a chemical formula that would allow anyone to recover from injury. As it involves chemical compounds, Matter 2, and since it involves living beings as well, Life 2 to 4 depending on the potency of the mixture.<br /> <br /> Ether Capsule: Nothing complex actually, using Prime 2 inserts quintessence into a capsule that can be opened to recharge the mage quickly, of course it must be prepared in advance, not sure if it also needed Matter to function.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>You are running into a common hazard in that you are mixing up the foci and the effect. You are adding how the foci works to how the Mage is altering the world with it. It's not wrong to do that, per se, but there's no game reason to do it and it arbitrarily penalizes some character concepts over others. It might be worth getting into for the big magic rituals, but not for day to day magic.<br /> <br /> In general, ignore how the casting works and limit your calculations to the effect the mage is pushing on himself or the world. So, assuming all of these are foci for the Etherite to cast with and not Devices or Trinkets:<br /> <br /> The railgun is just manipulating the kinetic energy of the slug, That's really a Forces 2 effect. You could argue that the slug starts with no kinetic energy so you need Forces 3/Prime 2, but I wouldn't because we don't argue that way for other kinetic applications.<br /> <br /> The rocket backpack is flight. That's a basic Forces 2 (for human sizes) for manipulating kinetic energy locked to either the backpack itself or the wearer. Forces 2/Matter 2 or Forces 2/Life 2. <br /> <br /> The restorative mixture is purely Life, though what level of life depends on the degree of change and if the Mage is altering himself or others. (if it is a trinket you have to have Prime 2)<br /> <br /> The Ether Capsule is not a foci at all but, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, is refined Tass. Prime 4 when the Etherite creates it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T12:20:39-07:00","id":1509076,"title":"","content":"For an Etherite mixing instruments and effects can be part of the fun of the Tradition, because they are techno-mages. But you still want to take existing technology and improving it with Science! if you're going that route, over doing more of the hard-line separation as Ramnesis suggests (which is a completely valid way to go too).<br /> <br /> What remains true is what Ramnesis said in that what counts the most is how your mage is altering the world around them. The SoE has members that to both &quot;altering impractical technology to make it practical,&quot; and, &quot;altering more fundamental things with a technological dressing,&quot; types in its ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T01:12:17-07:00","id":1509148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509027#post1509027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rocket backpack is flight. That's a basic Forces 2 (for human sizes) for manipulating kinetic energy locked to either the backpack itself or the wearer. Forces 2/Matter 2 or Forces 2/Life 2.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The backpack I guess should be Forces 3 or 4, because it's really hard to move a object with the weight of a human with a little motor, but you can do it if you can use combine with gravity control, but that is unleast Force 3, I really guess that no need to use Matter or Life in this case because I not altering any of their properties.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T01:23:38-07:00","id":1509150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509017#post1509017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the faction of this Tradition Mage of the Society of the Ether ? Adventurer, Progressivist, or some different group ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess should be adventurers or a variation of Ethernaut hardly the other factions have a reason to make something out of a research or anything much freaked out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T02:04:52-07:00","id":1509151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509007#post1509007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While none of these are entirely off-base, there's cleaner ways to handle most of them.<br /> <br /> Rail-guns: Rail-guns don't shoot electric blasts, so you might just need to rename this. A rail-gun, as the name implies, propels an armature down rails, and as the armature stops at the end of the rails, the projectile continues on having gained momentum from sitting in the armature. There are also coil-guns where the electromagnetic field used to accelerate is also used to suspend the projectile; negating the need for an armature or physical rails. These are real things we already have. The most important tool a SoE has to making a functional rail-gun weapon, is Matter. The biggest issue in rail-gun technology in multiple applications is the force of the magnetic acceleration is so strong, rail-guns have to be huge just to avoid ripping themselves to pieces.<br /> <br /> So while some Forces would help make a rail-gun more practical, what you want to start with is some Ether science to cook up some exotic materials via Matter so the actually body of the weapon is light enough to use, and strong enough to be fired more than once. After solving that current tech can handle the rest enough to make a weapon.<br /> <br /> Now, a Scientist! might want to go above and beyond this into creating a plasma rail-gun, that shoots some form of plasma bolt instead of a solid slug. Then you're going to need Forces and Prime to generate your ammo because we have no idea how to do that at human-weapon scales.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are points to consider and test. I prefer to use it with Prime myself to avoid having to worry about getting or producing ammo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509007#post1509007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rocket-packs: So, again, you don't need Prime, because we have rockets (though really you're probably going to want to use jet-packs in how they actually operate). Again, Matter is your friend because one of the reasons these aren't &quot;real&quot; yet is the material engineering side of things more than the physics side of things. One of the biggest problems with making a jet-pack a reality, is carrying enough fuel, so using Matter to vastly increase how much fuel your pack holds without increase weight is going to get you a functional pack better than constantly tried to use Forces and Prime to generate thrust. Matter also helps you make a flight suit that will keep your legs from burning off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's better to use Prime in this case, because it's more viable than using fuel, because the intention is not to make something for everyone to use so I wouldn't need to worry about creating the fuel, besides I would have to use a lot more quintessence of this form. Matter could be used in creation, but I don't think it will be necessary in final use.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T02:21:47-07:00","id":1509153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509076#post1509076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an Etherite mixing instruments and effects can be part of the fun of the Tradition, because they are techno-mages. But you still want to take existing technology and improving it with Science! if you're going that route, over doing more of the hard-line separation as Ramnesis suggests (which is a completely valid way to go too).<br /> <br /> What remains true is what Ramnesis said in that what counts the most is how your mage is altering the world around them. The SoE has members that to both &quot;altering impractical technology to make it practical,&quot; and, &quot;altering more fundamental things with a technological dressing,&quot; types in its ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure about that? From what I've read of them they're more pseudo-scientist than anything else for the level of absurdity of their inventions. It seems that their gadgets are not something made to be functional, but to be their focus to use their abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T04:06:30-07:00","id":1509162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509151#post1509151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are points to consider and test. I prefer to use it with Prime myself to avoid having to worry about getting or producing ammo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one of the big advantages of rail- and coil-guns is they can use a ridiculously large number of things as projectiles (rail-guns in particular can fire anything that fits, coil-guns ammo needs to be something that responds to magnetic fields).<br /> <br /> And using Prime is literally producing ammo, it's a rather inefficient method of doing so at that. Etherites are, of course, prone to cool over practical, but at that point you might as well stick with the classic ray-gun variant of your choosing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's better to use Prime in this case, because it's more viable than using fuel, because the intention is not to make something for everyone to use so I wouldn't need to worry about creating the fuel, besides I would have to use a lot more quintessence of this form. Matter could be used in creation, but I don't think it will be necessary in final use.<br /> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure, &quot;I made super-science jet fuel in my lab that can power my jet-pack for an hour of maximum thrust flight,&quot; is a lot more viable than, &quot;I need to cast Prime every few turns, and if I fail a roll I crash.&quot;<br /> <br /> You keep adding Prime to create something out of nothing... for things that aren't hard to get the base components of and in some cases are all around us all the time. And as Ramnesis pointed out, Forces can let you fly without Prime, because you have kinetic energy in yourself you can manipulate with Forces to fly. Prime doesn't add anything useful to the equation. You add Matter or Life to&quot;lock on&quot; the Forces effect so you don't have to concentrate on both maintaining the effect and piloting at the same time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509153#post1509153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The Etherites are an extremely diverse group in how they approach their Science!-magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I've read of them they're more pseudo-scientist than anything else for the level of absurdity of their inventions. It seems that their gadgets are not something made to be functional, but to be their focus to use their abilities. </div> </div> </div>That's the stereotype, not the complete picture. And if you just want to use technological trappings for instruments, you should be following Ramnesis's Sphere advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T04:47:02-07:00","id":1509165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509162#post1509162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure, &quot;I made super-science jet fuel in my lab that can power my jet-pack for an hour of maximum thrust flight,&quot; is a lot more viable than, &quot;I need to cast Prime every few turns, and if I fail a roll I crash.&quot;<br /> <br /> You keep adding Prime to create something out of nothing... for things that aren't hard to get the base components of and in some cases are all around us all the time. And as Ramnesis pointed out, Forces can let you fly without Prime, because you have kinetic energy in yourself you can manipulate with Forces to fly. Prime doesn't add anything useful to the equation. You add Matter or Life to&quot;lock on&quot; the Forces effect so you don't have to concentrate on both maintaining the effect and piloting at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would only work if I manufactured one with Matter, besides I don't know how people usually play, but in the games I saw, people use the rule that the expense is only for activation, so I wouldn't need to recharge every few turns , a charge could even last a whole scene, but you're right, that would be complicated to balance and subject to intervention, better discard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509162#post1509162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the stereotype, not the complete picture. And if you just want to use technological trappings for instruments, you should be following Ramnesis's Sphere advice.</div> </div> </div> </div>This complicates things, so how is it that the world has not undergone a technological evolution? Even with the intervening Technocracy something had to pass.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T05:24:59-07:00","id":1509169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509076#post1509076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an Etherite mixing instruments and effects can be part of the fun of the Tradition, because they are techno-mages. But you still want to take existing technology and improving it with Science! if you're going that route, over doing more of the hard-line separation as Ramnesis suggests (which is a completely valid way to go too).</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, my advice is purely about the casting of the spell in the moment. Stories about the characters aquiring or magically creating exotic materials or fuel for their foci are good fodder. I just recommend against tacking on Matter because the foci is a mixture (unless it wasn't already a mixture), or Prime because the foci is generating flames (unless it is doing so without fuel). <br /> <br /> For those who want to dig into paradigms, practices, and what Mages believe (and for the record I highly recommend doing so), the Abilities Enhancing Magic rolls are another great way to do it.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe#post1508978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Portable railgun: Basically a weapon composed of a rifle-like cannon, powered by an ether battery on its back and capable of launching large electrical discharges, it would need Prime 2 to generate electricity and Forces from 2 to 4 depending on how much power you use.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I got so lost in the slug throwing railgun I didn't cover the electric gun. Yes, this would be Forces 3/Prime 2. You need to be at Forces 3 before you can convert primal energies to electricity.<br /> <br /> That said, if some enterprising Etherite wanted to make a revolver that used batteries instead of bullets, they could probably use Forces 2 to dramatically amplify the discharged electricity, and that would be Forces 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509148#post1509148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The backpack I guess should be Forces 3 or 4, because it's really hard to move a object with the weight of a human with a little motor, but you can do it if you can use combine with gravity control, but that is unleast Force 3, I really guess that no need to use Matter or Life in this case because I not altering any of their properties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces 2 covers up to the size of a single human-sized character or a small area and that tracks with the behavior of other Spheres so it makes sense. Forces 2/Life 2 is also one of the combinations given for flying and levitation in M20.<br /> <br /> Not every spell needs to be locked, but this one needs to stay on the pilot or the pack. If it doesn't he gets a one time push and thats it.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T08:27:15-07:00","id":1509192,"title":"","content":"On locking an effect:<br /> <br /> It's not difficult to cast a spell that stays in the area it was cast, that's natural. We also don't need to pay anything extra if the effects of the spell can move out of the area. Turn someone into a frog and the effects will continue for the duration even if they run away. <br /> <br /> Sometimes, though, you want the spell itself to travel with something or someone. In that case you need to lock it to a pattern using one of the Pattern Spheres (Forces, Life, Matter, and sometimes Spirit or Mind). If your spell already uses that sphere (say, a Life effect that follows someone around) great, you are covered. If not you have to add another sphere.<br /> <br /> So consider a spell that turns a shoe into chalk. That's Matter 2. The effect travels with the shoe, but not the spell itself. No locking is required.<br /> <br /> If instead you want to make every solid object that passes through an area into chalk, that's still Matter 2. The spell isn't moving, no locking is required.<br /> <br /> Now if you want to instead cast a spell that makes every solid object a person touches turn into chalk. That needs to be locked to him, so it is Matter 2/Life 2. Life is acting as the locking sphere.<br /> <br /> If instead you cast a spell so that his shoes turn every solid object they touch into chalk, that's back to Matter 2. You are arguably locking the spell to his shoes but you are already using Matter 2 so it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Your jetpack effect needs to travel with the pilot to be effective and the base Forces spell doesn't cover that, so you need a locking Sphere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T09:45:32-07:00","id":1509203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509192#post1509192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On locking an effect:<br /> <br /> It's not difficult to cast a spell that stays in the area it was cast, that's natural. We also don't need to pay anything extra if the effects of the spell can move out of the area. Turn someone into a frog and the effects will continue for the duration even if they run away.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, though, you want the spell itself to travel with something or someone. In that case you need to lock it to a pattern using one of the Pattern Spheres (Forces, Life, Matter, and sometimes Spirit or Mind). If your spell already uses that sphere (say, a Life effect that follows someone around) great, you are covered. If not you have to add another sphere.<br /> <br /> So consider a spell that turns a shoe into chalk. That's Matter 2. The effect travels with the shoe, but not the spell itself. No locking is required.<br /> <br /> If instead you want to make every solid object that passes through an area into chalk, that's still Matter 2. The spell isn't moving, no locking is required.<br /> <br /> Now if you want to instead cast a spell that makes every solid object a person touches turn into chalk. That needs to be locked to him, so it is Matter 2/Life 2. Life is acting as the locking sphere.<br /> <br /> If instead you cast a spell so that his shoes turn every solid object they touch into chalk, that's back to Matter 2. You are arguably locking the spell to his shoes but you are already using Matter 2 so it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Your jetpack effect needs to travel with the pilot to be effective and the base Forces spell doesn't cover that, so you need a locking Sphere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, isn't correspondence used instead of Life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T11:36:33-07:00","id":1509220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509203#post1509203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that case, isn't correspondence used instead of Life?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is that you are anchoring the spell to an object or person or other pattern, so you have to use the Sphere that covers that pattern. In this case the spell is anchored to a person so the anchor sphere is Life. <br /> <br /> Strictly speaking you can't use Correspondence as a locking Sphere because it isn't a pattern Sphere. Even if you could, though, Correspondence is the sphere of locations and distance, so it would only let you lock to a place. To make the Chalk Touch or Jetpack work you need to anchor to a person or thing. That's Life or Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T14:59:06-07:00","id":1509234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509165#post1509165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This complicates things, so how is it that the world has not undergone a technological evolution? Even with the intervening Technocracy something had to pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems a fairly radical jump... but also the world has undergone a number of technological evolutions since the Etherites and Virtual Adepts left the Technocracy and joined the Traditions. Think about where technology was 120 years ago. The Etherites also claim to have specifically introduced both the Uncertainty Principle and quantum mechanics into the current Consensus to get back at the Technocracy for removing aether from it, making subatomic physics much much weirder, and completely changing the course of the Time Table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T16:23:25-07:00","id":1509325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509165#post1509165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This complicates things, so how is it that the world has not undergone a technological evolution? Even with the intervening Technocracy something had to pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, the Society of Ether lacks the ability to mass produce. Instruments are unique to the individual Etherite and can only be used by her; the same can be said of Inventions. Gadgets, Devices, and Trinkets can be used by others; but they have to be made individually (or in batches, in the case of Gadgets) by the Etherite. And the Devices require the Etherite to invest a bit of herself into it, in the form of Personal Quintessence and a point of permanent Willpower. <br /> <br /> The Technocracy <i>does </i>have mass production. That, and its Syndicate-provided reservoirs of Primal Energy, lets it fill up warehouses with Technological Wonders. Even Devices can be mass-produced, as the Technocracy found a way to make them without the personal investment I mentioned above. They're also far better equipped to \u201cTerranorm\u201d an area so that whatever innovations they deem appropriate to introduce get accepted into the Consensus. It's not that Etherites can't do these things (mostly); it's that the Technocracy is better at doing them on a large scale. <br /> <br /> That said, canonically the Etherites were responsible for Quantum Theory, not the Technocracy. So it's not like they haven't had any success in expanding the bounds of the Consensus. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T04:20:55-07:00","id":1509361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1508978-something-to-the-soe?p=1509325#post1509325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, the Society of Ether lacks the ability to mass produce. Instruments are unique to the individual Etherite and can only be used by her; the same can be said of Inventions. Gadgets, Devices, and Trinkets can be used by others; but they have to be made individually (or in batches, in the case of Gadgets) by the Etherite. And the Devices require the Etherite to invest a bit of herself into it, in the form of Personal Quintessence and a point of permanent Willpower.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy <i>does </i>have mass production. That, and its Syndicate-provided reservoirs of Primal Energy, lets it fill up warehouses with Technological Wonders. Even Devices can be mass-produced, as the Technocracy found a way to make them without the personal investment I mentioned above. They're also far better equipped to \u201cTerranorm\u201d an area so that whatever innovations they deem appropriate to introduce get accepted into the Consensus. It's not that Etherites can't do these things (mostly); it's that the Technocracy is better at doing them on a large scale.<br /> <br /> That said, canonically the Etherites were responsible for Quantum Theory, not the Technocracy. So it's not like they haven't had any success in expanding the bounds of the Consensus.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>One shared capability / quality is that both Etherite Tradition Mages and ( Iteration-X ) Technocrats can understand, comprehend, create, and use Primium, known in regard to it's details and qualities that make it simply an extremely, distinctly, and definitely : helpful and interesting temporal \\ solid substance or material.<br /> <br /> Also they might be involved in regard to simillar and comparable organisations, groups, agencies, businesses, industries, areas, lands, and regions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-23-2023, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}